  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## What listeners single out\n\n- **John Hardy** (1 other source): John Hardy flowed into The Gold Rush, with Billy playing as a duo with Victor Furtado [1]\n- **I'll Go Steppin' Too** (1 other source): Victor Furtado also joined in on I'll Go Steppin' Too [1]\n\n## Setlist highlights\n\n- **Salty Sheep**: rare: 7 archived performances [3]\n- **Come On Down The Mountain Katy Daley**: mythic rare: 2 archived performances [3]\n- **The Gold Rush**: rare: 10 archived performances [3]\n- **I'll Go Steppin' Too**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [3]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **billystrings2023-07-25.billystrings2023-07-25G-Man** (recommended): audience recording; 20 songs; 151 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Notes list a tune called Big Ball in Boston ahead of Salty Sheep, which opens the first set [1]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **billystrings2023-07-25.billystrings2023-07-25G-Man**: taped by G-Man; transferred by G-Man; source: Aud> Audio Technica AT-2020> Tascam 40 DX [1]",
